DESCRIPTION:Extreme environments place stringent demands on materials used
  in building construction and thermal insulation for a wide range of indus
 tries. In Arctic communities\, geographic remoteness leads to fragile supp
 ly chains\, energy-intensive production and transportation\, and unavoidab
 le end-of-life impacts. Climate change further intensifies these demands. 
 This seminar presents fungal biotechnology as an alternative to traditiona
 l building materials to address these challenges to human and planetary\n
